<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">New Netherland</h1><p class="st-meta">1614 CE – 1667 CE · capital New Amsterdam</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Dutch colony on the Hudson River, whose port of New Amsterdam became New York and whose tolerant, commercial character shaped the city.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-hudson">Henry Hudson</a> explored the river named after him for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1609, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> traders were soon buying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> there; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-netherland-company">New Netherland Company</a> built a post near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albany-new-york">Albany</a> in 1614. After 1621 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> took over, and in 1626 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-minuit">Peter Minuit</a> bought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The company governed through a director-general and council, and the colony lived on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-orange">Fort Orange</a>, with settlers drawn from many nations. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patroon">Patroonships</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rensselaerswyck">Rensselaerswyck</a> offered large estates to investors. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/willem-kieft">Willem Kieft's</a> war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a> in 1643 to 1645 nearly ruined the colony. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-stuyvesant">Peter Stuyvesant</a>, governing from 1647, conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-sweden">New Sweden</a> in 1655 and built the wall that gave Wall Street its name. Residents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flushing-queens">Flushing</a> protested his intolerance in 1657.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1664 an English fleet seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a> without a fight, and it became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-new-york">Province of New York</a>, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-breda-1667">Treaty of Breda</a> in 1667. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> briefly retook the colony in 1673 to 1674. Dutch place names and customs persisted in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-valley">Hudson Valley</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/new-netherland.jpg" alt="New Netherland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Miyamaki, Oren neu dag, Artem Karimov, Golradir · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prinsenvlag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1614 CE – 1667 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>New Amsterdam</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Peter Minuit, Willem Kieft, Peter Stuyvesant</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Church</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nieuw-Nederland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1640&amp;focus=new-netherland" aria-label="New Netherland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2866 724 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where New Netherland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3186 980L5097 634M3186 980L5097 634M3186 980L4970 663M3186 980L3186 980M3186 980L3136 1013M3186 980L3137 1011"/><path